p.src:
A known pure state has density operator $\rho_\psi=|\psi\rangle\langle\psi|,$ with eigenvalues $1,0,\ldots$, so $S(\rho_\psi)=0$. This does not mean that every measurement on $|\psi\rangle$ has a certain outcome. It means there is no additional statistical ignorance about the prepared state. At the opposite extreme, $\rho=\frac{I}{d}
\qquad\Longrightarrow\qquad
S(\rho)=\log d,$ where $d=\dim\mathcal H$. The maximally mixed state assigns equal weight to every orthogonal direction.

